Progress: Calendar round r4 Today halo overflow correction complete.

The Today halo has been rebuilt as an inset ring contained strictly inside the day cell box without rotating the element.

The previous halo pseudo element used `inset: -3px` and an element rotation that expanded the cell `scrollWidth` from 164 to 167. The updated rule sets `inset: 0` with 3px padding and mask compositing to form a 3px border ring directly inside the cell. A repeating linear gradient background-position sweep across 6 seconds now animates the highlight around the ring without element transforms, eliminating scrollable overflow.

### What works now
- Today day cell scrollable width and height remain completely flush with client dimensions (164px by 78px).
- The Today ring highlight sweeps along the inset border without any element rotation or layout shift.
- Still mode and reduced-motion overrides remain fully enforced.

### Changes made
1. [`calendar.css`](file:///Users/anthony/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-calendar/public/color-polish/scenes/calendar.css): Rebuilt `#tv .scene[data-scene="5"] .day.today::after` with `inset: 0`, `padding: 3px`, masked border box, and animated `background-position` from `200% 0` to `-100% 0` over 6s linear infinite; updated `@keyframes calendarTodayHalo` to animate `background-position`.
